      "content": "It's true that no one can magically erase your debt or fix your job situation instantly, and that makes the despair feel real. Instead of looking for a quick fix, consider what small, manageable steps you could take to reduce the pressure, even if it's just one tiny boundary at work. Sometimes, just shifting focus from \"fixing everything\" to \"surviving the next hour\" can create a tiny bit of breathing room in the loop.",
